From af332c565c87aa50bf364d27bfab7344d8c7a10f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LECH OS <dev@lech-os.invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Settings homepage: icons of LECH OS

The main screen of the system settings showed the icons of the base (a
tinted glyph on a coloured tile), while the settings app of LECH OS shows
its own icons (Pixel 9, 15. 11. 2026). The homepage tiles
(res/drawable/ic_homepage_*.xml, used by top_level_settings_expressive.xml
and the Kotlin screens) now show the LECH OS icons, which are complete
tiles: res/drawable-xxxhdpi/lech_set_*.png (160 px = 40 dp, the size of the
icon view). Tiles without a LECH OS icon (support, supervision, hub mode)
keep the icon of the base.
